// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/offer-a-new-version.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeOfferANewVersion(path: "/recipes/offer-a-new-version", title: "Offer a new version — Recipes", description: "When a deploy lands, offer the reader the new version of an offline site: update.available says it is ready, and update.apply() reloads into it.") {
    RecipeShell("Offer a new version", summary: "Tell the reader of an offline site that a new version has been deployed, and let them reload into it when they choose. This needs offline support turned on ([Make a site work offline](/recipes/work-offline)).  This home page offers a reload when a new version is ready, and shows how many changes are waiting to be sent:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Translate a site", to: "/recipes/translate-a-site"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Translate by the words as written", to: "/recipes/translate-by-the-words"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Publish a page in each language", to: "/recipes/site-in-two-languages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/offer-a-new-version.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** `offline` in `webfluent.app.json` ([Make a site work offline](/recipes/work-offline)) and a host that serves the site over HTTPS. It claims `/`: paste it into a new project, or replace the starter's `src/pages/Home.wf` with it.")
            CodeBlock(#"page Home(path: "/", title: "Home", description: "The front page.") {
    if update.available {
        Button("A new version is ready — reload") { on click { update.apply() } }
    }
    if network.queued > 0 {
        Text("{network.queued} change(s) will be sent when you are back online").muted
    }
    Heading("Home").h1
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("- **Every deploy is a version.** The worker is versioned by a hash of everything the build wrote, so any deploy that changes a byte is a new version.\n- **The new version waits.** It installs beside the old one and waits. `update.available` turns true when it is ready.\n- **`update.apply()` takes it** and reloads the page once. It never reloads on the first install, which only takes over a page that already works, and never twice for one update. The old version's store is deleted when the new one takes over.\n- **`network.queued`** is how many writes made offline are waiting ([Keep writes made offline](/recipes/keep-writes-made-offline)).")

    }
}
